# Coding standards

Follow `docs/coding-standards.md`.

- TypeScript strict; interfaces/types; no `any`.
- Idempotent TS and Next.js: pure functions, immutable data, pure renders, retry-safe GET.
- JS/TS naming: PascalCase for classes/types/interfaces/components; camelCase for values; kebab-case files.
- FP + DRY: compose small functions; extract shared domain logic.
- Style with Tailwind CSS. Stack is Next.js + React.
